Transformers (Moving Parts): license and attribution
=====================================================

This project contains a few kinds of material under different terms. All of
them are permissive; nothing here is NonCommercial. In short:

    Code                        MIT
      the application (src/), the exercises (skeletons, tests, solutions),
      the Python reference implementation, the brand components, and the
      tools/ scripts

    Prose and figures           CC BY 4.0
      the chapter text, the exercise prompts, the diagrams, and the course
      documents (CLAUDE.md, CASEBOOK.md, METHOD.md, BRAND.md, the design doc)

    Data                        public domain
      public/data/tinyshakespeare.txt is Shakespeare's text, public domain,
      in the concatenated form circulated by Andrej Karpathy's char-rnn
      repository (see tools/fetch_shakespeare.py for provenance and hash)

    Third-party notices         THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
      the offline parity-fixture generator derives from nanoGPT (MIT,
      (c) Andrej Karpathy); its notice travels there


